-- title:
--   Gluing point-wise Galois representations into a Hecke–Galois datum
-- statement:
--   Write $\mathbb{T}=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$). The first hypothesis `hES` is a per-point input, quantified over all primes $p$, all levels $N\neq 0$, all finite $S\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ with $p\in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$, all characteristic-zero discrete valuation domains $\mathcal{O}'$ that are adically complete for $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}'}$ with finite residue field and $p\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}'}$, and all ring homomorphisms $\chi:\mathbb{T}\to\mathcal{O}'$: it asserts the existence of a ring $\mathcal{O}''$ with the same list of properties, an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra structure on $\mathcal{O}''$ that is module-finite with local and injective structure map, and a $\rho:$ [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) $\mathcal{O}''$ (a free $\mathcal{O}''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})=\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\simeq_{\mathbb{Q}}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}''}V$ satisfying the adic continuity condition) such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$ one has $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\chi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ over $\mathcal{O}''$, and such that $\rho$ is unramified at every prime $q\nmid N$ with $q\neq p$ (inertia in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $q$ acts trivially). Now fix $p$, $N$, $S$ as above, a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}$, adically complete with finite residue field $k=$ `ResidueField` $\mathcal{O}$ and $p\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, a ring homomorphism $\theta:\mathbb{T}\to k$, and a residual representation $\bar\rho$ over $k$ (rank $2$, factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$) which is absolutely irreducible and satisfies $\operatorname{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ at all Frobenii as above. Fix further a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $T$, module-finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$ with local structure map, and a ring homomorphism $\pi:\mathbb{T}\to T$ such that the residue of $\pi(t)$ is the image of $\theta(t)$ under the induced map of residue fields, $\mathcal{O}[\operatorname{range}\pi]=T$, every $\chi:\mathbb{T}\to\mathcal{O}$ reducing to $\theta$ factors as $\psi\circ\pi$ for some $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi:T\to\mathcal{O}$, and the composite of $\mathcal{O}\to T$ with the residue map of $T$ is surjective. The conclusion is that there is a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) $H$ for $N$, $S$, $\mathcal{O}$, $\theta$, $T$ whose structure map is $\pi$ itself — so in particular a rank-$2$ adic Galois representation $H.\rho$ over $T$ with $\operatorname{charpoly}(H.\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ at every Frobenius at a prime $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and with absolutely irreducible residual representation $k_T\otimes_T V$ — and such that $H.\rho$ is unramified at every prime $q\nmid N$ with $q\neq p$.
--
--   This is the gluing step in the construction of the Galois representation attached to a residually absolutely irreducible Hecke eigensystem over a complete local coefficient ring: the representations attached to the $\mathcal{O}$-valued points of $T$ are assembled, via their traces, into a single representation over $T$ with the prescribed Frobenius characteristic polynomials. It is used to produce the Hecke–Galois data in the flat and ordinary settings, and in the variant in which the per-point input is supplied for arbitrary coefficient homomorphisms.
